  "body": "Found during the bounded search of #3319 (2026-11-22).\n\n## What happens\n\nThe part-solid law (`crates/sim/src/verify/solid.rs:214-237`) judges each rapid against the part solid. When the tool body or its edge column meets the part, it pushes `Warning::RapidInStock { at: i }`.\n\nThat warning prints this text (`crates/sim/src/verify/types.rs:467-468`):\n\n`rapid move N travels through stock (below the clearance plane, or at it below the stock top)`\n\nThe text is wrong for this case:\n- The rapid can be vertical (a lift out of a pass, or a drop to a pass start).\n- The rapid can be at or above the clearance plane at one end.\n- The tool meets the part, not the uncut stock.\n\nThe user then reads it as a lateral G0 under the clearance plane. This is what happened in #3319.\n\n## How to see it\n\nHeadless, `camcraft-cli mcp`, on `origin/main` 835556814 and on v0.25.0 (7e2a8119c):\n1. `import_model` `testdata/models/fig8.step`; `add_tool` `EM-0800-4FL`; `fit_stock` box, sides `[5,5,5,5,0,2]`.\n2. `edit_tool` `{\"flute_len\": 10}`.\n3. `add_operation` \"2D Offset\" on the bottom face (Z 0), containment Outside. Clearance = Top of stock +10, Top = Top of stock +0, Bottom = Selection +1.5, Stepdown 10, Entry Helix r 1.6, `retract_z` null.\n4. `generate`, then `verify`.\n\nResult: `shank_hit` on moves 1406-1658 and 2194-2446 (the outer ring of levels 2 and 3), and `rapid_in_stock` on moves 1659, 2193 and 2447. Moves 1659 and 2447 are the vertical lifts to Z 32 at (-0.202, -33.998). Move 2193 is the vertical drop to Z 4 at the same point. Each lateral G0 of the posted program (a long-flute copy of the same path) is at Z 32.\n\nThe post is blocked, so the output is safe. Only the message is wrong.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A rapid that the part-solid law convicts gets a message that says the tool meets the part on a rapid, and that names the move.\n- `rapids.rs` keeps its text for a rapid through the stock.\n- A pin test in `crates/sim/tests/` shows the two texts on the two cases.\n- The MCP `kind` string and the UI severity stay correct for the new text.\n",
